=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: mswitch0
diagnosis_text:
The Campus 1 multilayer switch, mswitch0, has had its entire FRR/OSPF configuration wiped. Its `/etc/frr/frr.conf` is empty and `ospfd` is not running. As a result, mswitch0 holds only four kernel-connected routes (10.2.2.0/24 on br0, and VLAN SVIs 172.16.10.0/24, 172.16.20.0/24, 172.16.30.0/24) and has absolutely no routes to the Campus 2 subnets (10.5.0.0/24, 10.6.0.0/24).

Every Campus 1 PC (PC5–PC14) uses mswitch0 as its L3 default gateway (172.16.10.254 / 172.16.20.254 / 172.16.30.254 respectively). When a PC sends a packet toward 10.5.0.x or 10.6.0.x, it forwards it to mswitch0, which silently drops it because there is no matching route and no default gateway. Intra-campus traffic is unaffected because the source and destination VLAN subnets are all directly connected on mswitch0.

Router16, mswitch0's upstream router, is running OSPF correctly (network 10.2.2.0/24 area 0 and 172.30.1.0/24 area 0) and does have full OSPF routes to Campus 2 via router7. However, it shows no OSPF neighbor on its bond0 (10.2.2.0/24) interface toward mswitch0 — confirming the adjacency never formed.

Root cause: mswitch0's FRR configuration was wiped (frr.conf empty, ospfd not started), eliminating its routing plane entirely.

Corrective fix: Restore mswitch0's FRR OSPF configuration — start ospfd and configure `router ospf` with `network 10.2.2.0/24 area 0`, `network 172.16.10.0/24 area 0`, `network 172.16.20.0/24 area 0`, and `network 172.16.30.0/24 area 0`. This will re-establish the OSPF adjacency with router16, allow mswitch0 to learn routes to Campus 2, and restore inter-campus reachability.
=== END ===